    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="0751" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg675"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">671.116/61: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Owsley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-24T12:00:00+03:00">April 24,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 24—10:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. Referring to my telegram No. 6, April 20, 6 a.m., despatched via London.
                    Pending Department’s consideration my written reports may I acknowledge receipt
                    of Rumanian reply; note that suspension order does not prohibit all imports and
                    that goods in customs and in transit will be omitted; say reply has been
                    forwarded with request for further instructions; and request that in the
                    meantime authorities take note of unofficial summary of statement explanatory of
                    most-favored-nation principle broadcast by the Department, April 7th?<anchor
                        n="13" xml:id="d541-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Owsley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d541-f1" n="13" xml:id="d541-f1-content">
                <p>Reference is presumably made to the Department’s press releases of April 1 and 5.
                    For texts, see Department of State, <hi rendition="#italic">Press Releases</hi>,
                    April 6, 1935, pp. 212 and 218.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
